# Trivy ignore list; read from the repo root by `trivy fs` / `trivy image` (security-scan.yml).
#
# CVE-2023-54404 / GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5: zod 3.25.76 (fixed only in zod 4.6.6) -- DoS when validating
# oversized constrained collections. zod is a transitive dependency only: puppeteer -> puppeteer-core
# -> chromium-bidi 17.0.2 (zod ^3.24.1), the WebDriver BiDi mapper. The scraper launches Chrome with
# puppeteer's default CDP protocol and never sets protocol 'webDriverBiDi' (puppeteer-core selects
# BiDi only on that option, or for Firefox by default); it never calls puppeteer.connect; and nothing
# in src/ or packages/ imports zod. The fix needs the puppeteer + Chrome bump, which is its own unit
# (the image pins Chrome to puppeteer's revision).
# Verified 2026-10-26; review by 2026-11-09 (puppeteer + Chrome bump unit). Expires on that date.
CVE-2023-54404 exp:2026-11-09

# CVE-2026-118664 / GHSA-qr28-fpjm-wq7f: decode-uri-component 0.2.2 (fixed in 0.5.1) -- quadratic-time
# DoS in the fallback decoder. Only path: minio 8.0.7 -> query-string 7.1.3 -> decode-uri-component.
# query-string calls the decoder only from parse/parseUrl/pick/exclude/stringifyUrl; minio calls only
# query-string.stringify, and nothing in src/ or packages/ imports query-string or decode-uri-component.
# No compatible fix exists: minio 8.0.7 is the latest release and still pins query-string ^7.1.3;
# decode-uri-component >=0.4.0 is ESM-only, so query-string 7's require() gets a namespace, not a
# function (parse throws; jest cannot load minio); query-string >=8 has only a default export, so
# minio's `import * as qs` loses qs.stringify (statObject throws). Verified 2026-10-29; expires
# 2026-11-12 (re-check minio releases, or replace minio).
CVE-2026-118664 exp:2026-11-12
